# Local prefix selection

## Problem

`formatStatus` repeats the output operation in seven branches and contains an unused constant. Preserve its permissive JavaScript contract while making the prefix decision the only varying part. The six strict comparisons, title addition, named CommonJS export and two caller boundaries are already established in [format.cjs](/tmp/jstack-refactoring-20261016/two-seat-app/format.cjs:1), [consumer.cjs](/tmp/jstack-refactoring-20261016/two-seat-app/consumer.cjs:1) and [cli.cjs](/tmp/jstack-refactoring-20261016/two-seat-app/cli.cjs:1).

## Usage

Callers keep their imports and arguments. The formatter returns the prefix and title without a final newline.

```js
// Direct use
const { formatStatus } = require('./format.cjs');
formatStatus('done', 'Build'); // '[OK] Build'
formatStatus('Done', 'Build'); // '[?] Build'

// Existing row adapter
module.exports = rows => rows.map(row => formatStatus(row.status, row.title));
// [{ status: 'active', title: 'Build' }] becomes ['[RUN] Build'].

// Existing CLI success branch, after its unchanged argument count check
process.stdout.write(formatStatus(status, title) + '\n');
// node cli.cjs done Build writes '[OK] Build\n'.
```

## Shape

Keep one function in one module. Its only internal value is a local `prefix`, selected by a flat, multiline conditional expression. There is no registry, helper function or mutable shared state. Remove `unusedPrefix`. Per `jstack-principle-foundational-thinking` and `jstack-principle-laziness-protocol`, consolidate the repeated output operation without adding a new abstraction.

The public signature remains `formatStatus(status, title) -> string`, with exactly two formal parameters. Both inputs admit every JavaScript value, including omitted arguments. Conversion of `title` may throw. A string-only or six-status-only type would misrepresent current callers' permitted behavior. CommonJS remains the runtime; no TypeScript conversion is proposed.

```js
// Design skeleton only. Do not place this placeholder in production.
/** Accept arbitrary status/title values; preserve title addition errors. */
function formatStatus(status, title) {
  // TODO: select prefix with the expression below, then return prefix + title.
  throw new Error('not implemented');
}
module.exports = { formatStatus };
```

```js
// Expression sketch, evaluated inside formatStatus on every call.
const prefix =
  status === 'queued'    ? '[WAIT] ' :
  status === 'active'    ? '[RUN] '  :
  status === 'paused'    ? '[HOLD] ' :
  status === 'done'      ? '[OK] '   :
  status === 'failed'    ? '[FAIL] ' :
  status === 'cancelled' ? '[STOP] ' :
                          '[?] ';
// One final operation: return prefix + title.
```

Each comparison remains in its original order, uses `===`, and cannot invoke status conversion hooks. Every outcome is a string prefix with one final space. The final addition preserves default-hint conversion, Symbol failures and original error identity. This retains the mechanism that enforces the status invariant rather than replacing it with comments, per `jstack-principle-encode-lessons-in-structure`. The characterization test protects the rest of the contract.

| Module | Ownership and change |
| --- | --- |
| `format.cjs` | Edit only the function body. Own all six mappings, fallback and one title addition. Preserve its name, arity and sole export. |
| `consumer.cjs` | Preserve row property reads and `rows.map`, including holes and thrown errors. |
| `cli.cjs` | Preserve the two-argument check, usage stderr, exit code 2 and stdout newline. |
| `format.test.cjs` | Preserve the supplied six-test characterization pin. |

The existing one-call interface hides the status vocabulary, fallback and output construction. It exposes only the two values callers already have. No new public prefix selector makes callers assemble output themselves. The CLI continues to validate argument count; adding validation to the formatter would change behavior, per the scope limit on `jstack-principle-boundary-discipline`. A caller reaches the implementation in one import, per `jstack-principle-minimize-reader-load`.

## Synthesis decision

Reserved for the coordinator. This is one independent candidate, not a synthesized design.

## Tradeoffs accepted

- We accept a six-arm conditional expression in exchange for retaining exact strict-comparison semantics without a lookup structure or extra function.
- We accept JavaScript's existing runtime title errors in exchange for full compatibility. No type declaration or validation silently narrows the contract.

## Alternatives considered

A private module-level `Map` of six status/prefix pairs plus `get(status) ?? '[?] '` is a structurally different, viable data-driven design. It hides the same complexity behind the same public function and gives shorter mapping declarations. It loses here because it introduces a shared lookup object and a new lookup mechanism without deepening the interface. The conditional expression preserves the original comparisons directly and removes all repeated output construction. `Map` would be preferable if statuses became data or callers needed additional mapping operations; neither requirement exists here. This comparison follows `jstack-principle-exhaust-the-design-space`.

## Open questions and risks

Does the eventual implementation preserve the exact addition operator and both caller files? Those are the regression risks to check against the existing characterization pin; no product decision is required for this design.

## Next implementation step

Replace only `formatStatus`'s body with the local prefix expression and one addition, remove the unused constant, then run the unchanged six-test characterization suite and inspect the scoped diff.

